pport a  free democracy of sovereign democracy  like ukraine and do everything we can  it's it's it's such a barbaric situation  what we're seeing with what putin has  done this it's absolutely important  so how what do you think we're going to  do keep on doing what we're doing more  sanctions more military aid  is that what we're going to do  yes look we've i think we're leading the  world at the moment in terms of  sanctions and putting that pressure on  the uh the russian economy  one of the shames of this is this you  know the russian this is not about the  russian people it's about putin's regime  and what he is doing and we've got to  put the pressure on them  and show that their invasion will not  work will have  negative impacts on  on their regime those sanctions that  we've put in over a thousand people and  and businesses across evolved with  russia  has that effect the support we have  given and again we led the way the  defense sector and the prime minister  very much leading the way at the very  early stages of that uh lethal defense  support that we have put into  um ukraine which they have been very  grateful and put into very good use to  defend themselves and as i say i'm very  proud that a big a big part of that has  been something that's come from uh the  people and businesses in northern  ireland that are producing uh that  weaponry to give ukraine the support  that it needs  let's talk about partygate and um scan  news understands those first finds have  been sent out by email we still don't  know to who do you think we will ever  know who has been fined who will be  fined and do you think we should we have  a right to know  well i i i don't know what um  individuals they they will do will do  the prime minister's been very clear  actually and uh that if the prime  minister were to be fined he would be  he would go public with that he'd be  open about that uh when fires were  issued across a range of things that the  the police work on uh that they don't  put that in the public domain it's a  matter for individuals that's just a i  know the individuals involved in this  are able to benefit from the same uh  rule of law that anybody else would if  they were fine that's a matter for them  i don't know before you ask  who hasn't has me fine but i can confirm  that if the prime minister fined that he  would make that public and just the  prime minister  well so it's a matter for individuals  what we don't know as well when we talk  about these fines is whether it's a  number of people or a number of fines  i've seen  because obviously  people could have more than one finance  we don't know the details of that the  obviously the met police themselves are  still continuing their investigation  when that completes we'll then have a  final concluding report from sue gray to  complete the work that she did obviously  she published that first stage report  before the metropolitan police  investigation really got underway and  that's the point of which we'll have the  full facts to be able to have a wider  conversation about what happened but as  i say the prime minister as i said  before has already previously outlined  his apology to people for what happened  how things were handled uh but we've got  to let the met police and the sue grey  complete their work to get that that  full  picture okay mr lewis thank you so much  for talking to us my pleasure

